"try":"Identify modes by ear."}]},{"t":"Intervals","lessons":[{"t":"Interval Number","learn":["Count letter names inclusively: C to F is a fourth.","Simple intervals are within an octave; compound intervals are larger (a ninth is an octave plus a second).","Melodic intervals are sequential; harmonic intervals sound together."],"check":[["C to F is a...","Fourth","Third","Fifth"],["A ninth is an octave plus a...","Second","Third","Ninth"],["Notes sounding together form a ___ interval.","Harmonic","Melodic","Compound only"]],"try":"Name ten intervals by number."},{"t":"Interval Quality","learn":["Perfect: unison, fourth, fifth, octave. Major/minor: second, third, sixth, seventh.","Augmented intervals are a half step larger than perfect or major; diminished are smaller than perfect or minor.","The tritone (augmented fourth or diminished fifth) spans six half steps."],"check":[["C to E is a ___ third.","Major","Minor","Perfect"],["C to E♭ is a ___ third.","Minor","Major","Diminished"],["A tritone spans ___ half steps.","Six","Five","Seven"]],"try":"Build major and minor thirds on five notes."},{"t":"Hearing Intervals","learn":["Link intervals to familiar songs to recognise them by ear.","Perfect fifths sound open; minor seconds sound tense.","Interval inversion: a third inverts to a sixth; major becomes minor."],"check":[["A major third inverts to a...","Minor sixth","Major sixth","Perfect fifth"],["Minor seconds sound...","Tense","Open","Empty"],["Perfect fifths sound...","Open","Clashing","Silent"]],"try":"Identify ten intervals by ear."},{"t":"Compound Intervals","learn":["Larger than an octave.","A 9th is an octave plus a 2nd.","Common in jazz chords."],"check":[["A 9th is an octave plus a...","2nd","3rd","5th"],["A 10th is an octave plus a...","3rd","2nd","4th"],["Compound intervals are larger than an...","Octave","Unison","Fourth"]],"try":"Name compound intervals."},{"t":"Interval Inversion","learn":["Flip the notes.","Numbers add to 9.","Major becomes minor; perf